<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"><title>Privacy and cookies | ClubManager</title><style>body{max-width:48rem;margin:3rem auto;padding:0 1.2rem;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18263b}a{color:#164d9d}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}</style></head><body><main><h1>ClubManager privacy and cookie notice</h1><p>ClubManager is an academic demonstration. Please use sample information and do not submit sensitive personal information.</p><h2>Information used by the demo</h2><p>Account creation asks for a username, email address and password. The app also stores account roles, optional profile pictures, messages, event registrations, announcements and event information entered through the app. These records are used to provide the corresponding club features. Passwords are stored as hashes by the account code.</p><h2>Cookies and external services</h2><p>The PHP session cookie supports sign-in and session state. The <code>club_notice</code> cookie remembers acceptance of the demo notice for up to 180 days. You can remove these cookies using your browser settings; removing the notice cookie will show the notice again. The application code reviewed does not include optional analytics or advertising cookies.</p><p>The interface requests fonts from Google Fonts, so Google receives a request from your browser when those fonts load. The application is hosted on Render and connects to a database; hosting and infrastructure providers may process technical information such as IP addresses and server logs.</p><h2>Questions and requests</h2><p>For questions about information submitted to this demo or to request its removal, contact <a href="mailto:aziz@azizkouki.com">aziz@azizkouki.com</a>. Retention periods and provider-side logging depend on the deployed configuration.</p><p><a href="/public/index.php">Return to the demo</a></p></main></body></html>
